From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: agent <agent@local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 02:05:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - translate block collision boxes without
 allocating on a miss

getCollisionsForBlocksOrWorldBorder is fourth on the CPU list under real
AI load, and AABB.move is its largest callee and the second largest
allocation site in the whole profile.

The single-AABB path called move() to translate the block's collision box
into world coordinates and only then tested it against the query box.
move() returns a new AABB, so every candidate block allocated one -- and
most candidates fail the test, so most of those were discarded
immediately. checkOnly callers discarded theirs even on a hit.

The translation is six additions. Both intersection tests already have an
overload taking the bounds as doubles, so the test now runs against those
and an AABB is constructed only on the path that keeps it.

Semantics are unchanged: same operands, same epsilon, same order, and the
retained box is built from the same six values move() would have
produced.

diff --git a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/collisions/CollisionUtil.java b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/collisions/CollisionUtil.java
index bc91b87da9c8034fc142007bfb0be4927bd958d6..17d1a7f5ae9ea7713a93b2dc72b93210b6ab6107 100644
--- a/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/collisions/CollisionUtil.java
+++ b/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/patches/collisions/CollisionUtil.java
@@ -2022,21 +2022,34 @@ public final class CollisionUtil {
                                         blockCollision = blockData.getCollisionShape(world, mutablePos, collisionShape);
                                     }
 
-                                    AABB singleAABB = ((CollisionVoxelShape)blockCollision).moonrise$getSingleAABBRepresentation();
+                                    final AABB singleAABB = ((CollisionVoxelShape)blockCollision).moonrise$getSingleAABBRepresentation();
                                     if (singleAABB != null) {
-                                        singleAABB = singleAABB.move((double)blockX, (double)blockY, (double)blockZ);
+                                        // SourbyCraft start - translate as coordinates, allocate only on a hit
+                                        // move() returns a new AABB, and this allocated one per candidate
+                                        // block before testing it. Most candidates fail the test, so most of
+                                        // those allocations were discarded immediately -- AABB.move is the
+                                        // second largest allocation site in an entity profile with players
+                                        // connected. The offset bounds are six doubles; both intersection
+                                        // tests already have an overload that takes them.
+                                        final double movedMinX = singleAABB.minX + (double)blockX;
+                                        final double movedMinY = singleAABB.minY + (double)blockY;
+                                        final double movedMinZ = singleAABB.minZ + (double)blockZ;
+                                        final double movedMaxX = singleAABB.maxX + (double)blockX;
+                                        final double movedMaxY = singleAABB.maxY + (double)blockY;
+                                        final double movedMaxZ = singleAABB.maxZ + (double)blockZ;
 
                                         // Not using the epsilon violates the collision rules but this is what Vanilla does.
                                         // Check BlockCollisions.class
                                         if (blockCollision == Shapes.block()) {
-                                            if (!aabb.intersects(singleAABB)) {
+                                            if (!aabb.intersects(movedMinX, movedMinY, movedMinZ, movedMaxX, movedMaxY, movedMaxZ)) {
                                                 continue;
                                             }
                                         } else {
-                                            if (!voxelShapeIntersect(aabb, singleAABB)) {
+                                            if (!voxelShapeIntersect(aabb, movedMinX, movedMinY, movedMinZ, movedMaxX, movedMaxY, movedMaxZ)) {
                                                 continue;
                                             }
                                         }
+                                        // SourbyCraft end - translate as coordinates, allocate only on a hit
 
                                         if (predicate != null) {
                                             if (!predicate.test(blockData, mutablePos)) {
@@ -2048,7 +2061,9 @@ public final class CollisionUtil {
                                             return true;
                                         } else {
                                             ret = true;
-                                            intoAABB.add(singleAABB);
+                                            // SourbyCraft - the only path that keeps the box, so the only
+                                            // path that needs one. checkOnly returns above without allocating.
+                                            intoAABB.add(new AABB(movedMinX, movedMinY, movedMinZ, movedMaxX, movedMaxY, movedMaxZ));
                                             continue;
                                         }
                                     }
